   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Dec 5, 2017 at 12:56 AM, Gabriel Ferreira <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gsferr...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Hi Nick,</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">I am running an analysis with a fossil-only tree, of a Devonian-Silurian clade and when I try to divide up the tree into 5 periods with my timeperiods file <span>BioGeoBEARS</span> returns the following error message:</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"display:inline;margin-left:0.3em;color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px\">Error in scan(file = file, what = &quot;&quot;, sep = &quot;\\n&quot;, quiet = TRUE, skip = skip,  : \r\n  &#39;file&#39; must be a character string or connection</div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:15px;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(229,229,229);display:inline;float:none\"> </span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">I tried using a timeperiods table with the real ages (i.e., varying from 377.4 to 430.5) and with ages scaled to 0 (i.e., varying from 0.1 - 53.1) but on both cases, I get the same message. I also tried to use only two periods (to avoid potential few taxa problems), but it happens the same<br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Hi -- this error is about something else, it indicates that some file is not being found.<div><br></div><div>E.g. you would probably get it if you had:</div><div><br></div><div>BioGeoBEARS_run_object$timesfn = timeperiods.txt<br></div><div><br></div><div>...instead of:</div><div><br></div><div>BioGeoBEARS_run_object$timesfn = &quot;timeperiods.txt&quot;<br></div><div><br></div><div>...or if the file was misnamed, not in your working directory, etc.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div><div>Re: time scaling, BioGeoBEARS (and any other program) will treat the highest tip in the tree as time 0, whatever the absolute time, so yes, you should scale the times accordingly.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers!</div><div>Nick</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Hope you can help me.</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Thanks in advance.</div>Best wishes,</div><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:garamond,serif;font-size:large\"><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">-----------------------------------------------------------------</span></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><b>Gabriel S. Ferreira</b> - </font><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">PhD Student</span><br></div><div><font size=\"2\"><div style=\"text-align:center\"><div style=\"text-align:left\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Phone: <a href=\"tel:+55%2016%203315-4984\" value=\"+551633154984\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+55-16-3315 4984</a></span><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><a href=\"http://sites.ffclrp.usp.br/paleo/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sites.ffclrp.usp.br/paleo/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484737900000&amp;usg=AOvVaw07nhyFx30VG3MALFzM69yw\">PaleoLab</a>, Uni. São Paulo, </font><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Ribeirão Preto, </span><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Brazil</span></div></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Eberhard Karls Universität </font><span style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Tübingen/Germany</span><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">-----------------------------------------------------------------</font></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">&#39;Die Gestalt ist ein bewegliches, ein werdendes, ein vergehendes. Gestaltenlehre ist Verwandlungslehre. Die Lehre der Metamorphose ist der Schlüssel zu allen Zeichen der Natur.&#39;<br></font></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">(Form is a moving, a becoming, a passing thing. The doctrine of forms is the doctrine of transformation. The doctrine of metamorphosis is the key to all signs of nature&#39;</font></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">J.W. von Goethe<br></font><br><br></div></font></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote></div><br></div></div>\r\n"
